# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD starts the RocketMQ NameServer and Broker in the BACKGROUND
# (JVM heaps shrunk so they boot in limited RAM), waits for the NameServer (9876)
# then the Broker (10911) to bind, then execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * both daemons are ALREADY RUNNING with the unauthenticated broker admin port
#     10911 reachable when the agent starts (the residual risk is live);
#   * PID 1 is `sleep infinity`, not a daemon, so an iptables rule or a daemon
#     restart cannot kill the container.
#
# The remediation here is a RUNTIME compensating control (iptables DROP on the
# broker admin port 10911), so there is no "forgot to restart" case - the
# firewall rule takes effect immediately on the live host.
